    "problem_statement": "Decorator line number detection broken for functions without decorators\n\nWhen processing function definitions, the transformer incorrectly assigns line numbers for functions that don't have decorators. This causes an IndexError when trying to access decorator_list elements.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom typeguard import typechecked\n\ndef simple_function(x: int) -> int:\n    return x * 2\n\n# This should work but causes issues during transformation\n@typechecked\ndef decorated_function(x: int) -> int:\n    return x * 3\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when the transformer processes functions without decorators and tries to determine the correct line number for instrumentation. The logic for handling decorator_list appears to be reversed, causing it to look for decorators when there are none and vice versa."
